**Plan: parse the flag in `cli.js`, add `toJson` to `format.js`.**

One fork to settle. `buildRows()` carries `owner` and `slow`. The table drops both on purpose. JSON has no width limit. So I would print the full row.

```js
// format.js
function toJson(rows) { return JSON.stringify(rows, null, 2); }

// cli.js
const flags = argv.slice(1);
const bad = flags.find((f) => f !== '--json');
if (command !== 'report' || bad) { process.stderr.write(USAGE + '\n'); return 1; }
const render = flags.includes('--json') ? toJson : toTable;
process.stdout.write(render(buildRows()) + '\n');
```

`USAGE` becomes `usage: cli.js report [--json]`.

